> The countries the highest per capita damages are generally rich, such as the USA, Saudi Arabia, and Canada. These countries have expensive assets at risk and high willingness to pay for non-market goods. However, poorer countries such as Nigeria and Pakistan have per capita damages that are very high for their income levels.
